by nicolas-grekas at 2026-09-02T15:23:10Z

One more round pushed on top of your work, @aschempp:

- `UserGuestAuthorizationCheckerInterface` is renamed to `GuestAuthorizationCheckerInterface`, and it now extends `UserAuthorizationCheckerInterface`. PHP allows widening a parameter type in an extending interface, so the two names describe one contract instead of two unrelated ones, and a checker that accepts a guest is a user authorization checker by definition.
- That relation closes a gap. `SecurityExtension::getFunctions()` registers `is_granted_for_user()` and `access_decision_for_user()` for `UserAuthorizationCheckerInterface` only, so a checker implementing just the guest interface got no Twig function at all, while `isGrantedForUser()` had been widened to accept it. A test covers this now.
- The Twig extension is back to a single `instanceof` check plus a null-user check, and `AuthorizationChecker` and `Security` name one interface again. The container still aliases both names, so either can be autowired.
- The interface docblock and `Security::isGrantedForUser()` now say what a null user means.
- Rebased on 8.2.

